    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "A data science team invites HIM to the kickoff for a model that will predict which inpatients need a CDI query. What is the most valuable thing you contribute in that first meeting?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Calculating the model's sensitivity and specificity against a holdout sample of charts",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Explaining how each proposed input field is actually captured, what it means in this organization, and where it is known to be unreliable",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Confirming the model's output will be stored in a HIPAA-compliant environment with access controls",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Approving the vendor contract and setting a realistic go-live date for the CDI department",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Provenance, capture rules, definitions, and reliability are things only HIM can supply, and they determine whether the model is learning about patients or about workflow. The tempting wrong answer is the performance-metric option — those numbers matter, but the analytics team can compute them, and a strong metric on a field that means \"nobody scrolled to screen two\" is a confident wrong answer. Privacy controls are necessary but do not make the model valid.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Who answers which question at the kickoff?</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"150\" width=\"440\" height=\"330\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"280\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">DATA SCIENCE OWNS</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Model selection</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Performance metrics</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Validation design</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"380\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Retraining schedule</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"432\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Taught in the analytics</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"462\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">book, not this one</text><rect x=\"600\" y=\"150\" width=\"440\" height=\"330\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"820\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">HIM OWNS</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Provenance of inputs</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Capture rules</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Local definitions</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"380\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Known soft spots</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"432\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Nobody else in the room</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"462\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">can answer these</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"520\" width=\"920\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"575\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">THE TRAP</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"622\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Strong metrics computed on a field that really</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"658\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">means \"nobody scrolled to screen two\"</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"730\" width=\"920\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"785\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">PRIVACY CONTROLS ARE REQUIRED</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"832\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">but they never make a model valid</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"910\" width=\"920\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"962\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">Validity starts upstream, in the record.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1002\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">That is where you already work.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Dividing the kickoff questions between analytics and HIM"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "The Surface Area — and What Comes Next",
     "content": "Step back and look at how much of your department AI already touches. Not future-state. Now.\n\n• **Coding** — computer-assisted and autonomous code assignment\n• **CDI** — worklist prioritization and evidence surfacing for queries\n• **Ambient documentation** — notes drafted from the visit conversation\n• **Release of information** — request classification, record assembly, redaction support\n• **Prior authorization** — automation on both the payer and provider sides\n• **Denials** — denial prediction and appeal letter drafting\n• **Registries** — automated abstraction into cancer, trauma, and cardiac registries\n• **Privacy monitoring** — anomaly detection on record access\n\nThat is the map of this book. Each of those gets real attention in the lessons ahead, along with the regulation, the ethics, the vendor evaluation, and the governance structures that hold them together.\n\nAnd underneath all of it sits one argument, worth memorizing: **the organization needs someone who can tell whether the machine's output is right.** Not whether it ran. Not whether it was fast. Whether it is *right* — supported by documentation, consistent with the guideline, defensible in an audit.\n\nThat person is you. Nobody else in the building has the combination of clinical vocabulary, coding rules, data governance, and legal record expertise the job requires.\n\nNext, we go under the hood — what these systems actually do, in plain language, so a vendor claim never has to be taken on faith again.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">THE HIM AI SURFACE AREA</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Where AI already touches the department &#8212; and the book</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"140\" width=\"440\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">CODING</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"234\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Computer-assisted and autonomous</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"266\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">code assignment from the chart</text><rect x=\"600\" y=\"140\" width=\"440\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"650\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">CDI</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"234\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Worklist ranking and evidence</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"266\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">surfaced for the query</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"325\" width=\"440\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"377\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">AMBIENT DOCUMENTATION</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"419\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Notes drafted from the recorded</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"451\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">exam-room conversation</text><rect x=\"600\" y=\"325\" width=\"440\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"650\" y=\"377\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#14b8a6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">RELEASE OF INFORMATION</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"419\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Request classification, record</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"451\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">assembly, redaction support</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"510\" width=\"440\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"562\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">PRIOR AUTHORIZATION</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"604\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Automation on the payer side</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"636\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">and the provider side both</text><rect x=\"600\" y=\"510\" width=\"440\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"650\" y=\"562\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">DENIALS AND APPEALS</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"604\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Denial prediction and drafted</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"636\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">appeal letters</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"695\" width=\"440\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"747\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">REGISTRIES</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"789\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Automated abstraction into</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"821\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">cancer, trauma, cardiac data</text><rect x=\"600\" y=\"695\" width=\"440\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"650\" y=\"747\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">PRIVACY MONITORING</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"789\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Anomaly detection across</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"821\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">record access logs</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"890\" width=\"980\" height=\"165\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">THE THROUGH-LINE OF ALL 20 LESSONS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"993\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">The organization needs someone who can tell whether</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1029\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">the machine's output is right. That is the HIM professional.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Eight places AI already touches HIM — the map of this book"
     }
    }
